Z||000000||aubicon||03-04-2001||12:02 AM||||i was breaking down the rack and pinion assembly on my 86 and could not figure out it wasent looking rite, then i reolized that the assembly was from an 88. is it possible to just bolt up an 88 rack and pinion to an 86 or does the whole front suspension assembly have to be changed, oh ya, it doesent apear that there where any modifications made to any parts to make them fit. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Songman||03-04-2001||01:49 PM||||From what I have learned, you cannot bolt an 88 front suspension into anything other than an 88. Of course, with lots of mods anything can be done though.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
